WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.117 --> 00:00:01.040
- Hi, it's Rie.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:03.960
Today, I've been challenged
to take a popular food

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.620
and Make it Fancy.

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:08.320
Today's challenger is Alix.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.010
- Hey Rie, it's your best friend
in the entire world, Alix.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:13.660
So today I'm gonna challenge you to make

00:00:13.660 --> 00:00:17.690
one of my favorite candies
in the world fancy, M&amp;M'S.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:20.100
Last time I challenged you
to make Skittles fancy,

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.840
and you did an amazing job.

00:00:21.840 --> 00:00:25.010
I figured that M&amp;M'S are
like the chocolate equivalent

00:00:25.010 --> 00:00:25.843
of Skittles.

00:00:25.843 --> 00:00:26.910
I can't wait to see you,

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.920
I can't wait to see what you make me,

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:32.351
and remember to Make it Fancy.

00:00:32.351 --> 00:00:33.500
(mischievous music)

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:35.850
- M&amp;M'S, of course I've had it before.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:38.400
I feel like it's a little
bit too sweet for me.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:42.200
Good thing it's they are
little so you can stop

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.990
when you feel overwhelmed.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:45.820
I'm gonna have a quick sample

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:49.765
since I haven't tried
this for a long time.

00:00:49.765 --> 00:00:50.598
(M&amp;M'S crunching)

00:00:50.598 --> 00:00:51.660
I like the crunch.

00:00:51.660 --> 00:00:53.740
First few bites are great.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:56.220
Make your hands become rainbow.

00:00:56.220 --> 00:00:58.080
Somehow I like brown one the best.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:00:59.510
I want to make something

00:00:59.510 --> 00:01:02.030
I've never made in this show before.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:05.330
I got some great idea, and as always,

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:08.350
I'm excited to Make it Fancy.

00:01:08.350 --> 00:01:10.353
(upbeat music)

00:01:10.353 --> 00:01:11.223
All right, here's what I got.

00:01:11.223 --> 00:01:14.600
Strawberries, apricots, vanilla cookies,

00:01:14.600 --> 00:01:18.590
heavy cream, butter,
yogurt, avocado, almonds,

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.860
goat cheese, cherries, and milk.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:25.400
From the pantry I got
flaxseed, cocoa powder,

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:28.930
maple syrup, sweetened
condensed milk, baking soda,

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:31.460
brown sugar, dark
chocolate, white chocolate,

00:01:31.460 --> 00:01:36.460
cacao nibs, pistachio,
coconut oil, flour, salt,

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.250
powdered sugar, and brandy.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.450
Okay, let's get started.

00:01:41.460 --> 00:01:43.042
Make it Fancy.

00:01:43.042 --> 00:01:44.710
(mischievous music)

00:01:44.710 --> 00:01:46.490
First, combine dry ingredients.

00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:50.980
I have one cup of flour, one
fourth cup of brown sugar,

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:55.450
one teaspoon of baking
soda, half teaspoon of salt.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:58.160
Mix well with whisk.

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.630
And I have one cup of whole milk,

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.720
quarter cup of yogurt, mix well.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:09.720
One tablespoon of flaxseed,
one tablespoon of cacao nibs,

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:14.210
quarter cup of pistachio,
half cup of dried cherry.

00:02:14.210 --> 00:02:16.620
Since M&amp;M'S had so many varieties,

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:19.640
I'm going to use peanut M&amp;M'S for this.

00:02:19.640 --> 00:02:20.660
I'm adding one cup,

00:02:20.660 --> 00:02:24.480
and I'm using more different
kinds of M&amp;M'S later.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:26.780
- [Producer] Which do you
think was invented first?

00:02:26.780 --> 00:02:29.690
The chocolate M&amp;M or the peanut M&amp;M?

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:31.810
- I think chocolate, right?

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:32.643
- [Producer] Yes.

00:02:32.643 --> 00:02:33.476
Do you know the year?

00:02:34.650 --> 00:02:35.593
- 1947?

00:02:37.868 --> 00:02:38.828
- [Producer] 1941.

00:02:38.828 --> 00:02:40.597
- It seems like a lot of--

00:02:40.597 --> 00:02:42.010
- [Producer] All the good stuff.

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:46.253
- I was gonna say junk food
it's invented in 1940s.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.710
The year of junk food.

00:02:48.710 --> 00:02:52.450
Pour this batter in a loaf pan,

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:56.440
bake this at 350 degree for 50 minutes.

00:02:56.440 --> 00:02:59.980
Cool down to room temperature
and freeze it for a bit.

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:02.780
So we baked, and cooled,
and put in the freezer.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:04.890
The reason we put in the freezer,

00:03:04.890 --> 00:03:07.060
it is easier to cut thinly.

00:03:07.060 --> 00:03:09.590
There is a lot of hard ingredients,

00:03:09.590 --> 00:03:12.170
like nuts and dry fruits in it,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:14.450
so it's a little tough to cut.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:18.320
If you have a sharp knife or a
bread knife, it will do well.

00:03:18.320 --> 00:03:21.250
So lay them on the tray.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:22.950
This is not like other pastry,

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:26.390
it's not like cookies, or cream puff.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:27.870
So it doesn't expand,

00:03:27.870 --> 00:03:31.490
so you can actually put
pretty close each other.

00:03:31.490 --> 00:03:33.580
I'm going to finish cutting them.

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:38.580
Bake at 300 degree for 15 to
20 minutes until it dries out.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:41.010
One cup of heavy cream.

00:03:41.010 --> 00:03:43.620
So this time I'm using mini M&amp;M'S,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:45.340
'cause it will melt quickly.

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:49.070
Half cup, cook until everything melts.

00:03:49.070 --> 00:03:51.462
- [Producer] M&amp;M'S are the
most common eaten chocolate

00:03:51.462 --> 00:03:53.110
in space.

00:03:53.110 --> 00:03:54.300
- Kinda makes sense, right?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.140
'Cause it's everybody loves chocolate.

00:03:57.140 --> 00:03:59.420
I'm not interested going to space,

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:02.800
so the only thing you will
see it's like those planets

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.920
there it's not many things you can eat.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:09.050
We are living in such a beautiful planet,

00:04:09.050 --> 00:04:12.040
and we have so many choice,

00:04:12.040 --> 00:04:14.120
you can eat whatever you wanna eat.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.350
But if you are going to space,

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:20.350
you have to wear same
thing, and food is limited,

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:25.130
and there it's so many things
I haven't seen in this world,

00:04:25.130 --> 00:04:27.456
then why go to space?

00:04:27.456 --> 00:04:28.289
(Rie laughing)

00:04:28.289 --> 00:04:31.500
Everything is melted in heavy cream.

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:36.400
Put this M&amp;M'S and heavy
cream mixture into a blender.

00:04:36.400 --> 00:04:39.960
This is smell like a nice hot chocolate.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:44.620
I'm adding one avocado,
quarter cup of maple syrup,

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:49.360
two tablespoon of cocoa
powder, one pinch of salt.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:51.103
I'm going to blend this.

00:04:51.103 --> 00:04:52.888
(blender running)

00:04:52.888 --> 00:04:56.210
And pour, cool this to room temperature

00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.530
and chill in a refrigerator
at least 30 minutes.

00:05:00.530 --> 00:05:03.320
One cup of heavy cream in a small pot,

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:05.470
10 ounce dark chocolate.

00:05:05.470 --> 00:05:10.270
And now I'm using the regular
M&amp;M'S, adding six ounce.

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.730
Two tablespoon of butter.

00:05:12.730 --> 00:05:14.130
Mix it up.

00:05:14.130 --> 00:05:16.800
- [Producer] Do you know
what their slogan is?

00:05:16.800 --> 00:05:19.033
- Melting pot of chocolate.

00:05:19.033 --> 00:05:21.392
- Milk chocolate that melts in your mouth

00:05:21.392 --> 00:05:23.106
and not in your hand.

00:05:23.106 --> 00:05:24.277
- It melts.

00:05:24.277 --> 00:05:26.060
It's melt in your hand.

00:05:26.060 --> 00:05:30.440
M&amp;M'S doesn't need to be
melt completely for this one.

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:34.280
Take off from the heat,
transfer this into a bowl,

00:05:34.280 --> 00:05:37.510
add three quarter cup of pistachio,

00:05:37.510 --> 00:05:40.030
three quarter cup of almond,

00:05:40.030 --> 00:05:43.690
three quarter cup of
crushed vanilla cookie,

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:45.840
two tablespoon of brandy.

00:05:45.840 --> 00:05:50.400
Using spatula and mix
everything well combined.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.410
Put this in a refrigerator
about 30 minutes

00:05:53.410 --> 00:05:55.180
or until moldable.

00:05:55.180 --> 00:05:57.550
Chocolate mixture firmed up,

00:05:57.550 --> 00:06:01.020
so I'm going to divide this in half.

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:06.020
Put in a plastic wrap,
kinda shape it into a log.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:08.350
Twist the corner.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:13.220
And you kinda hold this
end, tie the corner.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:16.200
Press against on a flat surface,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.297
and make even thickness log.

00:06:18.297 --> 00:06:22.700
I'm gonna do one more, put
the mixture in plastic wrap,

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:26.220
cover with plastic, tie the corner,

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:28.200
and press against flat surface

00:06:29.273 --> 00:06:32.920
and make an even thickness log.

00:06:32.920 --> 00:06:37.070
Chill this until completely
firm, about one to two hours.

00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:39.570
Okay, so the chocolate
log it's completely firm.

00:06:39.570 --> 00:06:44.570
Spread powdered sugar in
a sheet pan, and unwrap.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:46.920
And cover with powdered sugar.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.920
Brush off excess with pastry
brush, and I'm going to slice.

00:06:52.100 --> 00:06:56.350
It has a lot of hard ingredients
like cookies and pistachio,

00:06:56.350 --> 00:06:59.750
so instead of slicing like a saw motion,

00:06:59.750 --> 00:07:04.750
you kinda press it and push
it down like guillotine.

00:07:04.890 --> 00:07:07.150
It's this how guillotine work?

00:07:07.150 --> 00:07:08.245
Probably.

00:07:08.245 --> 00:07:09.078
(Rie laughing)

00:07:09.078 --> 00:07:11.490
Just use the heel of your knife

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:14.250
and just use the gravity.

00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.540
I'm going to finish cutting this,

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:19.770
and we have plenty more things to do.

00:07:19.770 --> 00:07:21.580
I have double boiler,

00:07:21.580 --> 00:07:26.320
adding one and half
cup of white chocolate,

00:07:26.320 --> 00:07:30.340
seven ounces of sweet condensed milk,

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:33.580
and two tablespoon of butter.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:37.580
Mix it until everything
is completely melt.

00:07:37.580 --> 00:07:39.130
And I'm using double boiler

00:07:39.130 --> 00:07:42.410
because white chocolate is easy to burn,

00:07:42.410 --> 00:07:47.410
and also butter helps white
chocolate not get burnt.

00:07:47.740 --> 00:07:50.770
So I have a greased container,

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.170
and I'm going to transfer this.

00:07:53.170 --> 00:07:55.330
Ooh, nice texture.

00:07:55.330 --> 00:07:58.300
Chill this in the
refrigerator about three hours

00:07:58.300 --> 00:08:01.140
or until this become completely firm.

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:05.865
One cup M&amp;M'S, add in a food processor.

00:08:05.865 --> 00:08:07.362
(food processor running)

00:08:07.362 --> 00:08:09.882
(Rie laughing)

00:08:09.882 --> 00:08:12.962
We didn't expect they was
coming out from here, okay.

00:08:12.962 --> 00:08:15.620
(food processor running)

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:17.460
This looks good.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:20.290
Add in a mesh sieve and strain.

00:08:20.290 --> 00:08:22.410
I just want to use this dust,

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.320
so I'm going to put bigger
bits in a separate bowl.

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.870
So this is the chilled
fudge I just made earlier,

00:08:29.870 --> 00:08:33.350
sprinkle this dust over the fudge.

00:08:33.350 --> 00:08:35.970
And you want to coat this evenly.

00:08:35.970 --> 00:08:37.270
- [Producer] Are you a cheese snob?

00:08:37.270 --> 00:08:40.450
- I am not a cheese
snob, I'm a cheese lover.

00:08:40.450 --> 00:08:43.330
My Instagram account it's
thedessertsnob, but I'm not.

00:08:43.330 --> 00:08:44.531
Am I snob?

00:08:44.531 --> 00:08:46.024
(Rie laughing)

00:08:46.024 --> 00:08:46.924
Maybe.

00:08:46.924 --> 00:08:49.880
Put this in the refrigerator
until I'm going to use it.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:52.090
We still have so many things left.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:53.740
Double boiler going.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.930
I'm adding six ounces white chocolate,

00:08:56.930 --> 00:09:00.200
and one tablespoon of butter.

00:09:00.200 --> 00:09:01.420
While it's melting,

00:09:01.420 --> 00:09:05.530
I'm going to combine 6 ounces goat cheese,

00:09:05.530 --> 00:09:10.530
quarter cup of powdered sugar,
and two tablespoon of milk.

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:15.700
My white chocolate mix
it's nice and melted.

00:09:15.700 --> 00:09:20.220
Put this over to my goat cheese mixture.

00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:25.220
Put half cup of mini M&amp;M'S and
half cup of chopped apricots.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:30.590
Fold them into white chocolate mixture.

00:09:30.590 --> 00:09:32.980
So we are going to put
this in the refrigerator

00:09:32.980 --> 00:09:35.480
about 30 minutes until moldable.

00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:39.297
My white chocolate mixture
it's the texture I want it.

00:09:39.297 --> 00:09:42.510
And I'm going to use plastic.

00:09:42.510 --> 00:09:47.220
The texture you want it's
firm but not too firm.

00:09:47.220 --> 00:09:50.020
You can mold it as you want.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:53.230
So the texture you're
looking for is mashed potato.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:57.860
I was thinking about we
were stretching on a break.

00:09:57.860 --> 00:10:00.970
In Japan during summer break,

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.280
I don't know if the kids still do it.

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:08.280
We have to go to like a park
and do the exercise every day

00:10:09.390 --> 00:10:11.320
at eight or seven AM.

00:10:11.320 --> 00:10:14.060
And if you go there, you get a stamp

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:16.420
and you have to turn in to teacher

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.930
after the summer vacation.

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.660
- [Producer] Do you remember
what the exercises were?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.110
- Yeah, like I still remember.

00:10:22.110 --> 00:10:26.453
There's a lot of like this, and jumping.

00:10:28.038 --> 00:10:28.871
(Rie laughing)

00:10:28.871 --> 00:10:33.871
While I was exercising I
shaped it into a rectangle.

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:36.490
I'm going to put this in the refrigerator

00:10:36.490 --> 00:10:38.840
about two hours until firm.

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:43.840
Meanwhile all of our
crews is going to exercise

00:10:44.220 --> 00:10:45.480
for two hours.

00:10:45.480 --> 00:10:47.330
One cup of dark chocolate,

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:51.100
and one cup of mini M&amp;M'S crushed,

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:54.190
and two tablespoon of coconut oil.

00:10:54.190 --> 00:10:56.080
Melt this completely.

00:10:56.080 --> 00:10:59.280
Alix finally met my son.

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:01.060
She was super excited.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:02.800
He is confused.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.633
(Rie laughing)

00:11:03.633 --> 00:11:05.060
But she is great with kids.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:09.180
I was a little bit worried
that shell is gonna remain big

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.760
but it actually melted quite nicely.

00:11:11.760 --> 00:11:14.530
So I'm not gonna use
blender, I was going to,

00:11:14.530 --> 00:11:15.890
change the plans.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:20.000
Take off from the heat,
dip the strawberries.

00:11:20.000 --> 00:11:24.180
So this is classic chocolate
dipped strawberries,

00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:27.540
but it has M&amp;M'S shell in it

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:31.020
so it's going to have a nice crunch to it.

00:11:31.020 --> 00:11:34.420
It might be a nice
surprise when Alix try it.

00:11:34.420 --> 00:11:38.450
I added coconut oil into
this chocolate mixture

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:41.790
because it will hardened much quicker

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:43.490
than just using chocolate,

00:11:43.490 --> 00:11:46.990
and it is much easier
than tempering chocolate.

00:11:46.990 --> 00:11:49.920
Put this in the refrigerator
until chocolate hardens.

00:11:49.920 --> 00:11:52.550
And we are going to make
something very exciting.

00:11:52.550 --> 00:11:55.180
I'm going to start with chocolate salami.

00:11:55.180 --> 00:11:57.790
Kinda make it look like a river.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.450
Kinda wanna make it look a little natural.

00:12:00.450 --> 00:12:02.310
So I want to show the inside,

00:12:02.310 --> 00:12:05.304
so I'm gonna just cut the nice wedges.

00:12:05.304 --> 00:12:07.396
It's just look like cheese, it's crazy.

00:12:07.396 --> 00:12:08.410
(Rie laughing)

00:12:08.410 --> 00:12:09.470
Gonna look like a Pokemon.

00:12:09.470 --> 00:12:13.880
I think charcuterie board
is getting very popular,

00:12:13.880 --> 00:12:16.350
'cause yeah, who doesn't like
a good charcuterie board?

00:12:16.350 --> 00:12:18.450
And it's so fun.

00:12:18.450 --> 00:12:21.010
Like there is a lot of things to eat.

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:24.330
I'm thinking about color and shape,

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:28.010
but mostly I'm kinda doing freestyle.

00:12:28.010 --> 00:12:31.660
Most important thing is you
want to make the board full,

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:35.830
and also you want to put
odd number, not even number.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:37.960
So I'm adding three piece

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:41.080
of chocolate dip strawberry with M&amp;M'S.

00:12:41.080 --> 00:12:44.670
And M&amp;M chocolate dip, I have grapes.

00:12:44.670 --> 00:12:47.946
I like cut up fig 'cause it's pretty,

00:12:47.946 --> 00:12:50.180
and just put here and there.

00:12:50.180 --> 00:12:52.547
Some orange.

00:12:52.547 --> 00:12:56.060
Chocolate it's kind of dark and brown,

00:12:56.060 --> 00:12:59.150
so I kinda want to add
some like pop orange

00:12:59.150 --> 00:13:00.310
and other fruits.

00:13:00.310 --> 00:13:05.310
Peanut M&amp;M'S, think I wanna
just fill space with this guy.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:06.410
Just having fun.

00:13:06.410 --> 00:13:10.550
I think this is perfect
for Halloween for adults.

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:12.540
Like grown-up snacks.

00:13:12.540 --> 00:13:15.767
So I have this cookies I'm gonna put here.

00:13:15.767 --> 00:13:16.960
Apricots.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:20.210
Wow this is fun board, I
want to come this party.

00:13:20.210 --> 00:13:21.910
I'm inviting myself.

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:26.910
Finish with pretty edible
flowers, and we are done.

00:13:27.481 --> 00:13:30.314
(whimsical music)

00:13:49.346 --> 00:13:52.950
M&amp;M charcuterie board, very fun and fancy.

00:13:52.950 --> 00:13:55.198
Let's see what Alix thinks.

00:13:55.198 --> 00:13:57.605
(upbeat music)

00:13:57.605 --> 00:13:59.432
Open your eyes.

00:13:59.432 --> 00:14:00.515
- Oh my gosh.

00:14:01.437 --> 00:14:03.860
Is this a chocolate charcuterie board?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:04.779
- Yes.

00:14:04.779 --> 00:14:05.710
(both laughing)

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:06.806
- [Alix] Chocolate salami?

00:14:06.806 --> 00:14:07.639
- Mhm.

00:14:07.639 --> 00:14:08.823
- Oh my God, and what is this like a--

00:14:08.823 --> 00:14:10.030
- It's a brie.

00:14:10.030 --> 00:14:13.240
- You always know how to
do A plus presentation.

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:14.080
- Oh thank you.

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:18.010
- I wanna try one of
these and one of these.

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.060
I wanna try everything.

00:14:19.060 --> 00:14:19.893
- Feel like cutting cheese too.

00:14:19.893 --> 00:14:21.772
- You look like you're cutting cheese.

00:14:21.772 --> 00:14:22.605
(Rie laughing)

00:14:22.605 --> 00:14:23.438
You cut the cheese, eh?

00:14:23.438 --> 00:14:25.100
Cheers, salami cheers.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:25.933
Mm.

00:14:25.933 --> 00:14:26.766
- Oh yeah.

00:14:26.766 --> 00:14:27.640
- Wow, it's unique.

00:14:27.640 --> 00:14:29.230
It's a little tangy.

00:14:29.230 --> 00:14:30.063
Delicious.

00:14:30.063 --> 00:14:33.230
I would've never paired goat
cheese and M&amp;M'S together.

00:14:33.230 --> 00:14:34.063
What is this?

00:14:34.063 --> 00:14:35.210
Oh chocolate dipped strawberries?

00:14:35.210 --> 00:14:36.110
I didn't even realize.

00:14:36.110 --> 00:14:37.200
Oh, should we eat it like this?

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.707
Like we're in love.

00:14:38.707 --> 00:14:39.928
(both laughing)

00:14:39.928 --> 00:14:41.394
Mm.

00:14:41.394 --> 00:14:43.610
- Charcuterie cheese board.

00:14:43.610 --> 00:14:45.440
- Rie, charcuterie.

00:14:45.440 --> 00:14:46.962
- [Both] Charcuterie.

00:14:46.962 --> 00:14:51.083
- Rie made me a chocolate charcuterie.

00:14:53.280 --> 00:14:57.360
And I say yay, 'cause it was really amay.

00:14:57.360 --> 00:14:58.900
- Three, two, one.

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:00.050
- [Both] Make it Fancy.

00:15:01.350 --> 00:15:03.800
- And dancy, ayy,

00:15:03.800 --> 00:15:04.969
ayy,

00:15:04.969 --> 00:15:05.927
ayy.

00:15:05.927 --> 00:15:06.885
(Alix laughing)

00:15:06.885 --> 00:15:09.468
(upbeat music)

